cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "biomod2 SDM Runner: a bilingual Shiny front end for biomod2"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Ozdemir"
    given-names: "Serkan"
    affiliation: "Isparta University of Applied Sciences, Faculty of Forestry"
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9425-3724"   # <- kendi ORCID'inizi yazin
repository-code: "https://github.com/srknozdemir/biomod2-sdm-runner"
abstract: >-
  A bilingual (English/Turkish) Shiny graphical interface for the biomod2 R
  package. All modelling is performed by biomod2; this application provides
  a front end covering presence/absence, continuous (count, abundance,
  relative) and nominal (multiclass, ordinal) response types, literature-based
  parameter selection scaled to the data, ensemble modelling with MaxTSS
  thresholding, stacked species distribution modelling for potential species
  richness, and publication-format response curves. Applied settings, session
  information and package versions are recorded on every run to support
  reporting under the ODMAP protocol. Users should cite biomod2.
